From ff677ea9e6c95d60b4acdddf75a3114addb58c3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woahwhattheheck <293286387+woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:16:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] Cast: Fix remote playback session and command ordering

- Ending a session moves the receiver application to stopping. A PLAY
  that arrives before the stop is confirmed now launches the Default
  Media Receiver again afterwards, instead of attaching to the instance
  that is going away (its LOAD was dropped and the new session
  invalidated). Ending a session while the receiver is still launching
  stops it once it is attached, unless a new request wants it.
- PAUSE, RESUME, STOP and SEEK sent while the item is still launching or
  loading are applied when the LOAD reply arrives. They were acknowledged
  without effect, so for example a STOP right after PLAY let the media
  start anyway.
- Report every status change to the status update receivers, including
  changes caused by our own requests, the end of a session and a session
  replaced by START_SESSION.
- START_SESSION stops the media of the session it replaces (also when
  its LOAD was still in flight) and reports the old item as canceled.
- A failed LOAD no longer overwrites a canceled or invalidated item with
  an error, and failures say whether the request timed out, could not be
  sent or the connection was lost.
- "Stop casting" (UNSELECT_REASON_STOPPED) stops the receiver
  application remote playback runs on that route.
- Do not crash on a status update receiver extra of the wrong type, and
  only use ScheduledThreadPoolExecutor.setRemoveOnCancelPolicy on API 21+.
